## Source evidence and limits

Read [Harlow](https://arxiv.org/html/1409.1231), sections 6.2.3 and 6.10, especially equations (195)-(196): the semiclassical dictionary is distinct from a generic gravity construction; anchored homologous extremal surfaces and least-area selection are presented at leading order. This supports the restricted formulation, not its empirical truth.

Read [Almheiri et al.](https://arxiv.org/html/2006.06872), sections 6, 8 and 10, equations (6.2), (6.3), (8.2), (10.4), and section 11.2: the prescriptions extremize then minimize, use replica continuation, and retain unresolved contour, saddle-inclusion, cutoff and exact-state issues. The local model separately supplies its finite regulators, convergence and attained minimum. The source does not prove those local existence assumptions.

Read [Saad, Shenker and Stanford](https://arxiv.org/html/1903.11115), introduction and sections 6.1-6.3: the JT genus expansion has a nonunique matrix-integral completion; ensemble dependence and extension to fixed or higher-dimensional theories remain separate questions. This corroborates the remark's limitation. No whole-book or all-transitive-supplier audit is claimed. Published suppliers were read as prerequisite context and left unchanged; no defective published supplier was found in the assigned uses.

